{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789856029,"nonce":"nkKrhF3nb8Hg4hRHTMrVZdLEchg=","title":"Lua: a local named _ENV does not scope the globals inside it","message":"In the reference, a free name x inside the scope of local _ENV = t resolves to t.x (the closest _ENV upvalue or local). The frontend declares such a local as an ordinary local; free names keep going through the chunk's environment. locals.lua from 148 on and attrib.lua 320 and 442 rely on it (do local _ENV = {assert=assert}; assert(true) end; local _ENV \u003cconst\u003e = 11 then X = 1 must raise). Needs scope-aware resolution: when a local or upvalue named _ENV is visible at a use, bind the free name as a field of it (a new Binding variant) and lower reads and writes as index operations on that variable.","files":null}]}